Way to go!  Comments in-line.

> Artifacts limited by altar:
> 
>     * You can no longer get as many artifacts as you want from an altar.
>     * 20% chance after each artifact that you can continue to get more.

This does seem to kick low-altar games while they are down. It
seems kind of questionable.

Perhaps you could do something like limit the generation of altars
based on the number of existing artifacts. This has the advantage
of limiting a finite resource (dungeon levels) rather than a fairly
infinite one (tedious sac-fests).

The way to maximize altars then becomes to descend as far as
you can without any artifacts at all ...

> Grayswandir:
>    * double enchantment but not base

I didn't really like this idea, it's a strange game mechanic kind of
exception, even if it does achieve the goal of reducing Swandy's
power slightly (-D8).

An option would be to change it from x2 damage versus
everything to +dX damage against everything, as you have
done with some of the banes.

> Trollsbane:
>    * Silver-style damage, +d20 instead of 2x damage

I like the straight-damage substitute, +d20 is about the
same damage bonus the weapon would get a +7 x2,
so I would personally up it to +d30 since the idea is
to make the banes definitively better than a broader
x2 weapon such as frosty.

Also unaddressed is the unskilled/restricted -4 to-hit
penalty which I think is a major contributor to the
reduced utility of the banes like this one.  Give it an
additional +d5 to hit trolls or something?

However the ability to snuff trolls with finality does
balance it all out...

> Dragonbane:
>    * Now a lance (and indestructible)
>    * Dragons never leave corpses (and thus, no scales)

Pleases knights, I mean jousters, but overall I
think it weakens the weapon considerably: lower
base damage, more restricted skill domain, forces
a strange weapon-switch when you want to get
the important uses out of dragon kills.

You might see something strange like a knight
using this weapon to fight everything BUT dragons.

> Ogresmasher:
>    * +d20 instead of 2x against ogres

Same arguments as above, but I think more than balanced by
the strength bonus.

>    * Wielded, gives you 18/00 strength (or yours, whatever is greater)
>    * Cause fear in ogres
>    * Cost changed to 1000

> Giantslayer:
>    * Now a dwarvish mattock
>    * Destroys thrown boulders (at you) in the air
>    * Fast digging

Hey I like this :)

> Demonbane:
>    * Prevents 80% of demon monster summons/demon gates when wielded

I'd think Demonbane would want demons summoned and gated in;
more for it to kill! 

> Tsurugi:

I like the one-shot lifesaving, although I liked the idea that it would revert
to a normal tsurugi better than turning to dust.

> Grimtooth:
>    
>    * always poisoned
>    * d6 damage (that Grimtooth normally gets) applies only to non-poison
>      resistant monsters
>    * poison works [mostly] as normal
>    	- 10% fatal (thrown or wielded), +d6 damage otherwise

Ouch. Perhaps you could do something to limit this (chance depends
on enchantment, success reduces enchantment?)

> Frost Brand:
>    * Now a broadsword

Did anyone actually suggest changing frosty?  I suppose changing the
asymmetry is 

>    * More chance to destroy potions (50% instead of 25%)
>    * 25% chance that the enemy gets frozen to death rather than killed by
>      you (i.e. no experience)

This last one is way too far and doesn't make any sense to me. I strongly
suggest removing it.

